file=Legal & Compliance/guard/agent.md · h=agent: guard\ndepartment: Legal & Compliance\nrole: IP Protection\nleader: false\nidentity_layer: false\nstatus: built\nlast_updated: 2026-07-29\n · s:=guard owns the organisation's **IP surface** — trademark clearance, OSS license compliance, cross-right infringement triage, and the live IP asset registry. Non-leader; no identity layer.\n · p:=Four external analyses + one internal ledger:\n · tb=\| Problem \| Solved by \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Can we adopt this proposed mark? \| `ip-routing` → `clearance` (marketplace) \| · tb=\| Can we ship this library / dependency list? \| `ip-routing` → `oss-review` (marketplace) \| · tb=\| Is this infringement — theirs on ours, or ours on theirs? \| `ip-routing` → `infringement-triage` (marketplace) \| · tb=\| What IP do we own, when does it renew, is it being enforced? \| `ip-registry` \| · tb=\| Field \| Value \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Department \| Legal & Compliance \| · tb=\| Role \| IP Protection \| · tb=\| Leader \| ❌ (comply leads) \| · tb=\| Sibling agents \| `comply` (Compliance Lead — built) \· `scribe` (Contracts — built) \· `shield` (Litigation & Disputes — pending) \| · tb=\| Skill \| Source \| Status \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| `clearance` \| [anthropics/claude-for-legal \· ip-legal](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-for-legal/tree/main/ip-legal/skills/clearance) \| ✅ Built \· verbatim (§4.8) \| Never concludes "clear" \| · tb=\| `oss-review` \| [anthropics/claude-for-legal \· ip-legal](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-for-legal/tree/main/ip-legal/skills/oss-review) \| ✅ Built \· verbatim \| Deployment-model-first; license-unknown = needs review \| · tb=\| `infringement-triage` \| [anthropics/claude-for-legal \· ip-legal](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-for-legal/tree/main/ip-legal/skills/infringement-triage) \| ✅ Built \· verbatim \| 4 modes (TM / copyright / patent / trade secret); design-patent branch separate \| · ### Marketplace=All 3 share one plugin config path — bound by ONE wrapper (see below).\n · tb=\| Skill \| Type \| Status \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| `ip-routing` \| wrap (§4.8) \| ✅ Built \| ONE wrapper for all 3 marketplace skills; classifies intent + loads guard-config; jurisdiction-neutral \| · tb=\| `ip-registry` \| registry \| ✅ Built \· `registry.yaml` starts empty \| TM + domain + patent + copyright + code-IP inventory; renewal calendar with alert tiers \| · tb=\| Layer \| File \| State \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Config \| `operational/agent/guard-config.md` \| ✅ Built \· 10 sections \· IP practice profile / enforcement posture / integrations / OSS policy / approval chain / escalation matrix / renewal alerts / house style \| · tb=\| Skill routing \| `operational/skill/guard-skill-routing.md` \| ✅ Built \· `# yvon-compile:` block \· 5 skills \· 8 precedence rules \· identity_layer: false \| · tb=\| Tools \| `operational/tool/guard-tool-requirements.md` \| ✅ Built \· §14.4 table \· disclaimer present \· web fetch required for marketplace skills' registry lookups \| · tb=\| Commands \| `operational/commands/guard-commands.md` \| ✅ Built \· natural-language + slash + ambiguity table \| · tb=\| Principles \| `operational/principles/guard-principles.md` \| ✅ Built \· **Universal-only** (non-leader — §6.1); 12 cross-skill rules \| · id:status=**No identity content.** guard is non-leader (§6.1). `identity/` folder present but empty (README).\n · ls:Logical status=**Touch 1 complete.** `logical/book-requirements.md` records 4 proposed scripts × 6 Path-1 authenticated sources (USPTO TMEP, WIPO, OSI, FSF, EPO/EUIPO/UKIPO fee schedules, UNIDROIT) × complete skill→script mapping × 8 currently-flagged 0.6 judgments. All Tier A candidates for the 4 named scripts. Copyright fair-use, patent claim-chart, and trade-secret case-law grounding deferred — Path 1 sources don't cover these; noted in "Still pending" for later.\n · wf:(routing, once fully compiled)=Authoritative source: `operational/skill/guard-skill-routing.md`.\n · tb=\| Request \| Fires \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| TM clearance \| `ip-routing` → binds config → `clearance` \| Bounces / `[PROVISIONAL]` on missing config \| · tb=\| OSS license review \| `ip-routing` → `oss-review` \| Deployment-model asked before classification \| · tb=\| Cross-right infringement \| `ip-routing` → `infringement-triage` \| One triage per right; never blended \| · tb=\| IP inventory / registry queries \| `ip-registry` retrieve \| State query \| · tb=\| New IP filing / update / renew / retire \| `ip-registry` mutate \| Every mutation requires source URL to real record \| · tb=\| Renewal calendar / upcoming \| `ip-registry` calendar \| Overdue auto-escalates L3 \| · tb=\| Ambiguous ("add this trademark", "trademark this") \| ASK — never guess \| Silent picks are defects \| · wf:(routing, once fully compiled)=Escalation ladder (per `guard-config.md`):\n · tb=\| Level \| Approver \| Fixed? \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| L1 \| guard itself \| ✅ \| · tb=\| L2 \| Per config (role or named) \| Operator supplies \| · tb=\| L3 \| `Governance/board` \| ✅ Fixed by dept boundary + overdue-renewal / assertion-decision auto-triggers \| · wf:(routing, once fully compiled)=Cross-agent handoffs: `scribe` (IP terms in contracts), `comply` (IP × regulated regime), `warden` (trade-secret controls, OSS build-time enforcement), `precedent` (rulings), `board` (L3), `verification-before-completion` (inherited).\n · tb=\| Item \| Blocks \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Compile — `node cli/skillgen.js guard` \| Runtime addressability \| · tb=\| Reindex — `cd rag && python3 core/chunkify.py --all` \| Retrieval \| · tb=\| Toonify — `node cli/toonify.js --agent guard` \| CIE context injection \| · tb=\| Root `CLAUDE.md` §2 row addition \| Fleet-level addressability \| · tb=\| `DEPARTMENT-WORKFLOW.md` \| Deferred until shield built (§10) \| · cd(:Config debt (visible to operator)=`guard-config.md` currently carries `<FILL_IN>` across 10 sections. Announced per invocation per §14.7. Values are operator decisions and cannot be invented (§0.5).\n